==English==

===Etymology===
{{pseudo-loan|en|la}}, derived from a pseudo-Latin form of {{der|en|fr|compassionné}}, past participle of {{m|fr|compassionner||to feel sorry for}}. {{surf|en|compassion|-ate|id2=adjective}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/kəmˈpæʃənət/|a=UK,adjective}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-compassionate.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-compassionate.wav|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|/kəmˈpæʃəneɪt/|a=UK,verb}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-compassionate2.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Having, feeling or showing [[compassion]] (''to'' or ''toward'' someone).
#: {{syn|en|empathetic|sympathetic|ruthful}}
#: {{ux|en|The '''Compassionate''', the All-'''Compassionate'''}} (names given to God in [[Islam]])
#* {{RQ:Donne Anatomy|passage=As a '''compassionate''' [[turquoise|Turcoyse]] which doth tell<br>By looking pale, the wearer is not well,}}
#* '''1675''', {{w|Robert South}}, A Sermon preached at Christ-Church, in ''Twelve Sermons Preached upon Several Occasions,'' London: Thomas Bennett, 1692, p.{{nbsp}}574,<sup>[http://name.umdl.umich.edu/A60954.0001.001]</sup>
#*: {{...}} there never was any heart truly great and generous, that was not also tender, and '''compassionate'''.
#* {{RQ:Dickens David Copperfield|49|page=502|text=He was by nature so exceedingly '''compassionate''' of anyone who seemed to be ill at ease {{...}} that he shook hands with Mr. Micawber, at least half-a-dozen times in five minutes.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|author=w:Mohsin Hamid|title=w:The Reluctant Fundamentalist|location=Orlando|publisher=Harcourt|chapter=7|page=99|url=https://archive.org/details/isbn_9780739488263
|passage={{...}} the '''compassionate''' pangs I felt for soon-to-be redundant workers were not overwhelming in their frequency; our job required a degree of commitment that left one with rather limited time for such distractions.}}
#* {{RQ:Guardian|author=Richard Luscombe|title=Trump refuses to apologize for video with racist imagery of Obamas posted on his social media|date=2026-02-07|url=https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/feb/06/trump-racist-video-barack-michelle-obama|author2=Shrai Popat|author3=Robert Mackey|passage={{quote-gloss|Hakeem}} Jeffries hailed the Obamas as “brilliant, '''compassionate''' and patriotic Americans” and denounced Trump as “a vile, unhinged and malignant bottom feeder”.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260207071148/https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/feb/06/trump-racist-video-barack-michelle-obama}}
# Given to someone as an [[exception]] because of a family [[emergency]] or a death in their family.
#: {{ux|en|'''compassionate''' [[leave#Etymology_3|leave]]; a '''compassionate''' [[visa]]}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Inviting or asking for pity.
#: {{syn|en|piteous|pitiable|ruthful|Thesaurus:pitiful}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Richard 2|I|3|text=It [[boot#Verb_2|boots]] thee not to be '''compassionate''':<br>After our sentence [[plain#Verb|plaining]] comes too late.}}

